{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/915131-crossover-with-classic-wod-especially-mage-technocracy","id":915131,"title":"Crossover with classic WoD? (Especially Mage/Technocracy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T15:25:04-07:00","id":915131,"title":"Crossover with classic WoD? (Especially Mage/Technocracy)","content":"I've been feeling curious about that for some time: who here did ever try to crossover Promethean with some of the classic WoD games? And how did it go?<br /> <br /> I'm very tempted to add a Promethean NPC in a game I'll run sometime later this year\u2014more specifically, a Mage: the Ascension Technocray-oriented game. Not 1st ed, bad-to-the-bone Technocracy, mind you. More in a &quot;department tasked with investigating items causing troublesome manifestations&quot; kind (think &quot;snag, bag and tag&quot; in Warehouse 13), within a current-era Tech that hasn't fully recovered from the Revised metaplot.<br /> <br /> Obviously, since it's going to be a NPC, I won't go into every little detail, but I'm thinking it could be an interesting roleplaying challenge for the players. Among other things:<br /> <br /> &quot;Who is that person? Why do I feel a growing unease in their presence day after day, even though they're fairly nice? Wait, my Apparatus shows strange readings. I stand corrected: WHAT is that person? It doesn't look like any of the Reality Deviants we met and fought... Also do we act actively against them, leave them to another team, try to understand them and get them to join us...&quot; Etc. Because, well, all things said and done, that Promethean <i>wants</i> to be human, to leave their &quot;deviancy&quot; behind, to become part of the Masses (again), to &quot;redeem themselves and find a normal place again within the Consensus&quot;. And let's be honest, the Tech has its fair lot of cyber-enhanced operatives and other clones.<br /> <br /> So, did any of you try this (even if not in a Technocracy game, but with Tradition mages... or vampires... or other splats)?<br /> <br /> I'm not so much interested in the rules part\u2014adapting Attributes and Traits, difficulty threshold, with a bit of Rule of Cool thrown in it, that's not a real problem for me. I'm much more interested in the roleplaying aspect, and how smoothly (or not) this could be integrated. I know that first oWoD editions were a bumpy road to go in that regards, and Promethean itself, from what I recall of the books I read 4-5 years ago, feels more like a &quot;solitary&quot; game than one where you can add lots of other supernatural beings. So I expect this to be even trickier.<br /> <br /> Still... I'd like to give it a try. And see what others have done with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:07:39-07:00","id":915197,"title":"","content":"Prometheans would be kind of a funny thing in oWoD cosmology, since the Fire could reasonably be considered the Wyld personified, but their influence is more Wyrm-like, and their goals of rejoining humanity are really kind of pro-Weaver in some ways (unless I'm really misunderstanding the Triat and their motivations). Perhaps they are sort of a microcosm of the three?<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be pretty interested to see a translation guide for Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:04:21-07:00","id":915453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/915131-crossover-with-classic-wod-especially-mage-technocracy?p=915197#post915197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans would be kind of a funny thing in oWoD cosmology, since the Fire could reasonably be considered the Wyld personified, but their influence is more Wyrm-like, and their goals of rejoining humanity are really kind of pro-Weaver in some ways (unless I'm really misunderstanding the Triat and their motivations). Perhaps they are sort of a microcosm of the three?<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be pretty interested to see a translation guide for Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do something like Mummy or the Liminal Exalted - the Prometheans of the oWoD are given the Fire by a godlike figure to serve that figure's agenda, Possibly, like the Liminals, there needs to be a mortal intermediary to convey the Fire - someone trying to create life or resurrect the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:11:37-07:00","id":915549,"title":"","content":"I was in a game the other way around; players were Prometheans, but the world was oWoD. The supernatural NPCs we interacted with didn't know about Prometheans (not due to them being new, but due to them being rare), and there was a lot of violent poking the PCs involved (varying from the physical (werewolves), mental (vampire), and mystical (mage)). I think it worked pretty well thematically, but the ST avoided metaplot like the plague. When playing, we did downplay Wastelands and Disquiet as-written so we could actually stay in a town and do things; for an NPC, that might be less of a problem.<br /> <br /> From a Werewolf standpoint, I'd argue that Prometheans spring from an uncorrupted Wyrm as well as Wyld; while they do exist to change, they also embody the necessary entropy of a system. The Wyrm is about change, too, but its changes simplify and break down, rather than complicate and build up. Azoth is change, made of Elpis and Flux, creative and destructive. Elpis is Wyld, Flux is Wyrm, totally works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:45:17-07:00","id":915739,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, Frankenstein's Monster is already a character in owod, he's a son of ether. The good doctor was probably also a son of ether, but I don't remember the write up that well.<br /> <br /> I toyed with the idea of a created splat for owod, although my ideas didn't look like that much like promethean, although there were some similarities (lightning healing them, superhuman vitality and strength, some being nuclear powered, some being really pretty thanks to plastic surgery being far more advanced today than back then), but far more along the lines of the son of ether- Created fighting nazis while riding dinosaurs in the hollow earth, sword duels in a spaceship above Mars, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:37:04-07:00","id":915811,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the input. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I haven't decided on anything yet, but I may tweak down the Wasteland effect slightly (wouldn't make for long-term anything if the NPC has to leave every 2 weeks or so). Maybe find a middle ground: Disquiet (of course) and a milder version of Wasteland, with the PCs crossing paths with the NPC once too many\u2014and hopefully bound to wonder &quot;strange, every time we run after a new Deviant item, we see them in the area... Are they looking for the same thing, by chance?&quot; (Paranoia, thy name is... well, paranoia.)<br /> <br /> In any case, Prometheanswould be very rare in that game, indeed. The kind of rare that hasn't even been classified, and is only mentioned in some old report dating back to the 40s or something, as &quot;unidentified Deviancy, capture and study until we know more&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought yet about the Triat interpretation\u2014never STed, played or even read the WW rules, so while I know the concept behind it, I usually don't go too far with it. It's definitely interesting, all the more if considering the Wyrm aspect here as the uncorrupted one. Even though Technocrat characters wouldn't think in such terms, I'd be very disappointed if the players weren't intrigued by such a combination.<br /> <br /> I'm going to keep the godlike figure influence idea in store. I probably can't use something like that as &quot;end-series&quot; arc (if it goes too much into Spirits, Incarna etc. it may be a problem with such PCs), but as a background element? Sure. After all that being's agenda doesn't <i>have</i> to be related to the Chronicle itself, and they could be in the long game for something else, totally different. The NPC would simply happen to meet the PCs at some point.<br /> <br /> I do want to keep the &quot;journey towards humanity&quot; aspect, though. It's special enough in WoD to deserve attention. (There aren't many splats who'll gladly get rid of their powers to become a representative of Human: the Victim, eh? ^^)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:09:09-07:00","id":915864,"title":"","content":"Prometheans are a thing in the WoD, sort of: see the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook</b>, Revised Edition, where they are mentioned by name and are even given character creation rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:29:02-07:00","id":917340,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's one of the books I have, but only flipped through without reading much of it, shame on me (I ST Mage 2nd ed, although I'm going to switch to M20 for this upcoming Technocracy game). I'll have to get a look at this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://yzabel.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">Stuff I Draw</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">Lyo</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/938347-lyonesse-rising-the-story-of-an-avatar\" target=\"_blank\">nesse Rising [The Story of an Avatar]</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11810-zashiki-warashi","name":"Zashiki-warashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}